ARTICLE III — ABSOLUTE PROHIBITIONS

The following acts are absolutely and unconditionally prohibited with
respect to the Work, in whole or in part, without explicit written
authorization from the Sovereign:

  § 3.1  REPRODUCTION
         Copying, reproducing, duplicating, mirroring, archiving, caching,
         or storing the Work by any means or in any medium.

  § 3.2  DISTRIBUTION
         Distributing, publishing, transmitting, broadcasting, sharing,
         sublicensing, selling, renting, lending, or otherwise making the
         Work available to any third party.

  § 3.3  MODIFICATION
         Modifying, adapting, translating, transforming, augmenting,
         annotating, or creating derivative works based on the Work.

  § 3.4  REVERSE ENGINEERING
         Reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling, decoding, or
         otherwise attempting to reconstruct the source code, architecture,
         or logic of the Work from any compiled or distributed form.

  § 3.5  COMMERCIAL USE
         Using the Work, directly or indirectly, in connection with any
         commercial product, commercial service, revenue-generating
         activity, or competitive intelligence effort.

  § 3.6  AI TRAINING — ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION
         Using the Work, in whole or in part, as training data, evaluation
         data, fine-tuning data, reinforcement signal, preference data,
         distillation source, benchmark input, or in any other capacity
         in connection with the development, improvement, evaluation, or
         operation of any artificial intelligence, machine learning, deep
         learning, large language model, or statistical inference system.
         This prohibition is unconditional. It applies regardless of:
         (i)   commercial or non-commercial intent;
         (ii)  direct or indirect processing;
         (iii) transformative or verbatim use;
         (iv)  the technical method by which the Work is processed;
         (v)   whether the resulting system competes with the Sovereign.

  § 3.7  PATTERN EXTRACTION
         Extracting, reproducing, or reconstructing architectural patterns,
         design principles, algorithmic structures, or intelligence methods
         from the Work for use in any independent development effort.

  § 3.8  AUTOMATED ACCESS
         Accessing the Work through automated means, crawlers, scrapers,
         or any non-human process for any purpose.

