ARTICLE IV — TRADE SECRET DECLARATION

The Work constitutes trade secrets of the Sovereign.

The Sovereign has taken and continues to take reasonable measures to
maintain the secrecy and proprietary nature of the Work, including:
access controls, confidentiality obligations on authorized personnel,
technical protection measures, and sovereign licensing instruments
including this document.

Any person or entity who obtains the Work through any means — including
lawful access to a public repository — acquires it subject to the trade
secret obligations set forth herein. Such access does not constitute
authorization to use, disclose, reproduce, or exploit the Work.

Applicable trade secret law includes, without limitation:
  - Defend Trade Secrets Act, 18 U.S.C. § 1836 et seq.
  - Texas Uniform Trade Secrets Act, Tex. Civ. Prac. & Rem. Code § 134A

