ARTICLE VII — ENFORCEMENT AND REMEDIES

The Sovereign reserves all remedies available at law and in equity,
including but not limited to:

  (a) Preliminary and permanent injunctive relief without bond;
  (b) Actual damages, including lost profits, reasonable royalties,
      and full disgorgement of unjust enrichment;
  (c) Statutory damages under applicable copyright law, including
      enhanced damages for willful infringement;
  (d) Exemplary damages under the Defend Trade Secrets Act (up to
      two times the damages award for willful misappropriation);
  (e) Full attorneys' fees, litigation costs, and expert fees;
  (f) Criminal referral where applicable under 18 U.S.C. § 1832;
  (g) Any other remedy available under applicable law.

The Sovereign's election not to enforce any provision in any particular
instance does not constitute a waiver of any right under this instrument,
and does not establish a course of dealing that would limit any future
enforcement.

